# Refactoring Implementation Plan for Manga Prompt System

The goal is to refactor the existing manga prompt generation system ([manga_config.py](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/2nd-Brain/18_%E3%82%B7%E3%82%B9%E3%83%86%E3%83%A0/manga_config.py), [manga_utils.py](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/2nd-Brain/18_%E3%82%B7%E3%82%B9%E3%83%86%E3%83%A0/manga_utils.py), [smart_refactor.py](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/2nd-Brain/18_%E3%82%B7%E3%82%B9%E3%83%86%E3%83%A0/smart_refactor.py)) to improve code quality, maintainability, and readability, while preserving the existing functionality ("機能そのままで").

## User Review Required

> [!NOTE]
> I will assume `utf-8` encoding for all files moving forward, as modern Python/Windows handles this well with explicit encoding arguments. The original checks for ASCII-only will be replaced with standard UTF-8 handling.

## Proposed Changes

### System Core (`18_システム`)

#### [MODIFY] [manga_config.py](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/2nd-Brain/18_システム/manga_config.py)
- **Objective**: Separate configuration data from logic and improve readability.
- **Changes**:
    - Add Python type hints.
    - Move logic-heavy template formatting (like injecting `CHARACTER_SETTINGS` into `TEMPLATE` inside the config) to the consumer/utils, keeping config purely distinct constants.
    - Group constants logically (Paths, Character Data, Templates).

#### [MODIFY] [manga_utils.py](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/2nd-Brain/18_システム/manga_utils.py)
- **Objective**: Implement missing logic and provide robust utility functions.
- **Changes**:
    - Add type hints to all functions.
    - **Fix**: Implement a proper [get_safe_filename](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/2nd-Brain/18_%E3%82%B7%E3%82%B9%E3%83%86%E3%83%A0/manga_utils.py#46-48) function that actually sanitizes the string (instead of returning static "manga_file").
    - **Refactor**: Improve [extract_info_from_md](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/2nd-Brain/18_%E3%82%B7%E3%82%B9%E3%83%86%E3%83%A0/manga_utils.py#23-37) with more robust regex patterns.
    - **Refactor**: Improve [get_dialogues](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/2nd-Brain/18_%E3%82%B7%E3%82%B9%E3%83%86%E3%83%A0/manga_utils.py#38-45) to actually extract dialogue from content if possible, or return structured defaults.

#### [MODIFY] [smart_refactor.py](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/2nd-Brain/18_システム/smart_refactor.py)
- **Objective**: Refactor procedural code into a modular class-based structure.
- **Changes**:
    - Create a `MangaRefactorer` class to encapsulate state and logic.
    - Break down [process_single_file](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/2nd-Brain/18_%E3%82%B7%E3%82%B9%E3%83%86%E3%83%A0/smart_refactor.py#19-73) into smaller methods: `read_file`, `parse_content`, `generate_content`, `write_file`.
    - Remove unused variables (e.g., `TITLE_SAFE` if verified unused in template).
    - Ensure `dry-run` logic is clean and separated from effectful code.

#### [DELETE] [Legacy Wrappers]
- I propose keeping [update_all_manga_prompts.py](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/2nd-Brain/18_%E3%82%B7%E3%82%B9%E3%83%86%E3%83%A0/update_all_manga_prompts.py) and [refactor_prompts.py](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/2nd-Brain/18_%E3%82%B7%E3%82%B9%E3%83%86%E3%83%A0/refactor_prompts.py) as they are simple wrappers, but I will ensure they point correctly to the refactored [smart_refactor.py](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/2nd-Brain/18_%E3%82%B7%E3%82%B9%E3%83%86%E3%83%A0/smart_refactor.py). *No changes needed unless they break.*

## Verification Plan

### Automated Verification
I will create a temporary test script `tests/test_refactor.py` (or similar) to run the following checks:

1.  **Dry-Run Verification**:
    - Run `python smart_refactor.py --dry-run` on existing files.
    - Capture output and ensure no errors occur.

2.  **Regression Test**:
    - Create a sample `test_prompt.md` with known content.
    - Run the **original** [smart_refactor.py](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/2nd-Brain/18_%E3%82%B7%E3%82%B9%E3%83%86%E3%83%A0/smart_refactor.py) (backup logic) and save result.
    - Run the **refactored** [smart_refactor.py](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/2nd-Brain/18_%E3%82%B7%E3%82%B9%E3%83%86%E3%83%A0/smart_refactor.py) and save result.
    - Compare findings. *Note: Since "random scene" is selected, I will mock the random seed or check for structural equivalence rather than exact string match.*

### Manual Verification
1.  **User Verification**:
    - I will ask the user to run the refactored script with `--dry-run` on their actual folder to see if the logs look correct.
